{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-16980","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15315","text":"Skill 08 — Provider Implementation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-16982","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15316","text":"How to build a provider that satisfies a [&] Protocol capability contract. Registration, conformance testing, and MCP transport binding."}]}],"id":"blk-16981","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-16983","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15317","text":"Why This Matters"}]},{"id":"blk-16984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15318","text":"Capabilities are interfaces. Providers are implementations. The protocol is only as useful as the providers that satisfy its contracts. This file teaches you how to build one."}]},{"id":"blk-16985","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15319","text":"The Provider Concept"}]},{"id":"blk-16986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15320","text":"A provider is a service that implements one or more capability contracts. The [&] Protocol ecosystem includes default providers:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-16988","spans":[{"id":"spn-15321","text":"Provider"}]},{"id":"blk-16989","spans":[{"id":"spn-15322","text":"Capabilities Provided"}]}],"id":"blk-16987","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-16990","spans":[{"id":"spn-15323","text":"Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-16991","spans":[{"id":"spn-15324","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-15325","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15326","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.episodic"},{"id":"spn-15327","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15328","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-15329","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15330","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.attend"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16992","spans":[{"id":"spn-15331","text":"TickTickClock"}]},{"id":"blk-16993","spans":[{"id":"spn-15332","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-15333","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15334","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.forecast"},{"id":"spn-15335","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15336","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.pattern"},{"id":"spn-15337","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15338","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.baseline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16994","spans":[{"id":"spn-15339","text":"GeoFleetic"}]},{"id":"blk-16995","spans":[{"id":"spn-15340","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.fleet"},{"id":"spn-15341","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15342","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.geofence"},{"id":"spn-15343","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15344","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.route"},{"id":"spn-15345","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15346","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.region"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16996","spans":[{"id":"spn-15347","text":"Deliberatic"}]},{"id":"blk-16997","spans":[{"id":"spn-15348","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.argument"},{"id":"spn-15349","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15350","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.vote"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-16998","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15351","text":"But any MCP-compatible service can be a provider. The protocol is provider-agnostic by design."}]},{"id":"blk-16999","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15352","text":"Contract Conformance Requirements"}]},{"id":"blk-17000","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15353","text":"To satisfy a capability contract, a provider MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-17001","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15354","text":"1. Implement all declared operations"}]},{"id":"blk-17002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15355","text":"If the contract for "},{"id":"spn-15356","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-15357","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-15358","marks":["code"],"text":"detect"},{"id":"spn-15359","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15360","marks":["code"],"text":"enrich"},{"id":"spn-15361","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-15362","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-15363","text":" operations, the provider must implement all three."}]},{"id":"blk-17003","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15364","text":"2. Accept the declared input types"}]},{"id":"blk-17004","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15365","text":"Each operation specifies an "},{"id":"spn-15366","marks":["code"],"text":"in"},{"id":"spn-15367","text":" type. The provider must accept data conforming to that type."}]},{"id":"blk-17005","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15368","text":"3. Produce the declared output types"}]},{"id":"blk-17006","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15369","text":"Each operation specifies an "},{"id":"spn-15370","marks":["code"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-15371","text":" type. The provider must return data conforming to that type."}]},{"id":"blk-17007","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15372","text":"4. Respect accepts_from / feeds_into"}]},{"id":"blk-17008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15373","text":"The provider must accept input from the types listed in "},{"id":"spn-15374","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-15375","text":" and produce output consumable by the types in "},{"id":"spn-15376","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-15377","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-17009","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15378","text":"5. Expose operations via MCP transport"}]},{"id":"blk-17010","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15379","text":"Operations are invoked as MCP tools. The provider must respond to MCP tool calls over stdio or HTTP transport."}]},{"id":"blk-17011","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15380","text":"MCP Transport Binding"}]},{"id":"blk-17012","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15381","text":"Providers expose their operations as MCP tools. The binding maps contract operations to MCP tool names:"}]},{"id":"blk-17013","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Contract operation    →    MCP tool name\n─────────────────────────────────────────\ndetect                →    detect_anomaly\nenrich                →    enrich_context\nlearn                 →    learn_observation"},{"id":"blk-17014","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15382","text":"Tool registration"}]},{"id":"blk-17015","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15383","text":"When the provider starts as an MCP server, it registers tools that correspond to its contract operations:"}]},{"id":"blk-17016","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"detect_anomaly\",\n      \"description\": \"Detect anomalous events in temporal data streams.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"data\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"number\" } },\n          \"streams\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"data\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-17017","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15384","text":"Resource registration (optional)"}]},{"id":"blk-17018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15385","text":"Providers can also expose MCP resources for read-only state inspection:"}]},{"id":"blk-17019","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"resources\": [\n    {\n      \"uri\": \"provider://runtime/health\",\n      \"name\": \"Provider Health\",\n      \"description\": \"Runtime health status\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-17020","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15386","text":"Provider Registration"}]},{"id":"blk-17021","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15387","text":"To make a provider discoverable, register it in the capability registry."}]},{"id":"blk-17022","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15388","text":"Registry entry format"}]},{"id":"blk-17023","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"provider\": \"my-time-provider\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"capabilities\": [\"&time.anomaly\", \"&time.forecast\"],\n  \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n  \"command\": \"my-time-provider\",\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"contracts/v0.1.0/time.anomaly.contract.json\",\n    \"contracts/v0.1.0/time.forecast.contract.json\"\n  ],\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/org/my-time-provider\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-17024","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15389","text":"The registry is used by "},{"id":"spn-15390","marks":["code"],"text":"provider: \"auto\""},{"id":"spn-15391","text":" resolution and by the "},{"id":"spn-15392","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-15393","text":" command to verify that providers exist."}]},{"id":"blk-17025","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15394","text":"Testing Provider Conformance"}]},{"id":"blk-17026","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15395","text":"Contract validation"}]},{"id":"blk-17027","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15396","text":"Verify that your provider's MCP tool surface matches the declared contract:"}]},{"id":"blk-17028","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"# List your provider's tools\necho '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"tools/list\",\"id\":1}' | my-provider\n\n# Compare against the contract\nampersand validate-provider \\\n  --provider my-time-provider \\\n  --contract contracts/v0.1.0/time.anomaly.contract.json"},{"id":"blk-17029","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15397","text":"Integration testing"}]},{"id":"blk-17030","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15398","text":"Test that each operation accepts the declared input type and produces the declared output type:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-17032","spans":[{"id":"spn-15399","text":"Test"}]},{"id":"blk-17033","spans":[{"id":"spn-15400","text":"What to verify"}]}],"id":"blk-17031","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-17034","spans":[{"id":"spn-15401","text":"Input acceptance"}]},{"id":"blk-17035","spans":[{"id":"spn-15402","text":"Send each "},{"id":"spn-15403","marks":["code"],"text":"in"},{"id":"spn-15404","text":" type; verify no error"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17036","spans":[{"id":"spn-15405","text":"Output shape"}]},{"id":"blk-17037","spans":[{"id":"spn-15406","text":"Verify output matches "},{"id":"spn-15407","marks":["code"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-15408","text":" type"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17038","spans":[{"id":"spn-15409","text":"Wildcard compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-17039","spans":[{"id":"spn-15410","text":"Send output from "},{"id":"spn-15411","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.*"},{"id":"spn-15412","text":" provider; verify acceptance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17040","spans":[{"id":"spn-15413","text":"Error handling"}]},{"id":"blk-17041","spans":[{"id":"spn-15414","text":"Send invalid input; verify graceful error response"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17042","spans":[{"id":"spn-15415","text":"Side effects"}]},{"id":"blk-17043","spans":[{"id":"spn-15416","text":"Verify "},{"id":"spn-15417","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: true"},{"id":"spn-15418","text":" operations modify state"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17044","spans":[{"id":"spn-15419","text":"Idempotency"}]},{"id":"blk-17045","spans":[{"id":"spn-15420","text":"Verify "},{"id":"spn-15421","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: false"},{"id":"spn-15422","text":" operations are safe to retry"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-17046","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15423","text":"Common Implementation Patterns"}]},{"id":"blk-17047","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15424","text":"Pattern 1: Thin MCP wrapper"}]},{"id":"blk-17048","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15425","text":"Wrap an existing service (database, API, ML model) in an MCP server that maps contract operations to service calls:"}]},{"id":"blk-17049","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"MCP tool call → Provider → Existing service → Response → MCP result"},{"id":"blk-17050","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15426","text":"This is the simplest approach. Graphonomous wraps an Elixir/OTP application. A pgvector provider would wrap PostgreSQL."}]},{"id":"blk-17051","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15427","text":"Pattern 2: Multi-capability provider"}]},{"id":"blk-17052","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15428","text":"A single provider can satisfy multiple contracts. Graphonomous provides "},{"id":"spn-15429","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-15430","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15431","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.episodic"},{"id":"spn-15432","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15433","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-15434","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-15435","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.attend"},{"id":"spn-15436","text":" — all from one MCP server."}]},{"id":"blk-17053","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15437","text":"Register each capability separately in the contract, but serve them from one process."}]},{"id":"blk-17054","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15438","text":"Pattern 3: Stateless operation provider"}]},{"id":"blk-17055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15439","text":"Some capabilities are stateless — they transform input without maintaining state. These are simpler to implement and test:"}]},{"id":"blk-17056","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Input → Transform → Output (no state)"},{"id":"blk-17057","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15440","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-15441","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic: true"},{"id":"spn-15442","text":" flag in the contract signals this pattern."}]},{"id":"blk-17058","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15443","text":"Pattern 4: Provider with feedback loop"}]},{"id":"blk-17059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15444","text":"Providers with "},{"id":"spn-15445","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-15446","text":" operations accept outcome feedback and improve over time. This requires persistent state:"}]},{"id":"blk-17060","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Input → Process → Output\n                  ↓\n          Feedback → State update"},{"id":"blk-17061","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15447","text":"Mark these operations with "},{"id":"spn-15448","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: true"},{"id":"spn-15449","text":" in the contract."}]},{"id":"blk-17062","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15450","text":"Checklist: Shipping a New Provider"}]},{"id":"blk-17063","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17065","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15451","text":"Choose which capability contracts to satisfy"}]}],"id":"blk-17064","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17067","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15452","text":"Implement all operations declared in each contract"}]}],"id":"blk-17066","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17069","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15453","text":"Build an MCP server that exposes operations as tools"}]}],"id":"blk-17068","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17071","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15454","text":"Write a registry entry for discoverability"}]}],"id":"blk-17070","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15455","text":"Test conformance against the contract schemas"}]}],"id":"blk-17072","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17075","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15456","text":"Publish the provider (npm, hex, crates.io, or standalone binary)"}]}],"id":"blk-17074","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17077","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15457","text":"Submit a PR to add your provider to the registry"}]}],"id":"blk-17076","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierarp76523waz3deu7wgm3ztr6e6m5um3u32n7ltdjirehyrkufw4lq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}